### Q7: Handling Email Failures

**Jury might ask:** "What happens if the email service crashes while sending 1000 election result notifications?"

**Your answer:**

"Excellent question about reliability! Here's how we handle it:

**Scenario**: Email service crashes, 500 of 1000 result emails fail

**Without proper error handling (Bad):**
```
ElectionResultsPublishedEvent
├─ Send email to user 1 ✓
├─ Send email to user 2 ✓
├─ ...
├─ Send email to user 500 (CRASH! Email server down)
├─ Process hangs indefinitely
└─ Users 501-1000 never get email
   And we don't know which ones failed!
```

**Our Solution (Good):**
```java
@Component
@RequiredArgsConstructor
@Slf4j
public class ElectionEventListener {
    
    @Async
    @EventListener
    public void onElectionResultsPublished(ElectionResultsPublishedEvent event) {
        ElectionCall call = event.call();
        ElectionResults results = event.results();
        
        // Get all voting members
        List<User> voters = userRepository.findByVotedInElection(call.getId());
        
        for (User user : voters) {
            try {
                emailService.sendElectionResultsToUser(
                    user.getEmail(),
                    results.getSummary()
                );
                log.info(\"Email sent to {}\", user.getEmail());
                
            } catch (MailException | IOException e) {
                // Email failed, but don't crash
                log.error(\"Failed to send email to {}\", user.getEmail(), e);
                
                // Publish event for retry mechanism
                publisher.publishEvent(
                    new EmailFailedEvent(
                        user.getEmail(),
                        \"ElectionResultsNotification\",
                        event  // Original event to retry
                    )
                );
            }
        }
    }
}

// Retry mechanism (in separate listener)
@Component
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class EmailRetryListener {
    
    @Async
    @EventListener
    public void onEmailFailed(EmailFailedEvent event) {
        // Retry logic:
        // 1. Store failed email in DB
        // 2. Schedule retry (exponential backoff)
        // 3. After 3 retries, escalate to admin
        
        failedEmailRepository.save(FailedEmail.builder()
            .email(event.email())
            .subject(event.subject())
            .originalEvent(event.originalEvent())
            .retryCount(0)
            .nextRetryTime(
                LocalDateTime.now().plusMinutes(5)  // Retry in 5 min
            )
            .build()
        );
        
        log.warn(\"Email to {} added to retry queue\", event.email());
    }
}

// Scheduled retry task
@Service
@RequiredArgsConstructor
@Scheduled(fixedDelay = 60000)  // Run every 60 seconds
public void retryFailedEmails() {
    List<FailedEmail> toRetry = failedEmailRepository
        .findByNextRetryTimeLessThanAndRetryCountLessThan(
            LocalDateTime.now(),
            3  // Max 3 retries
        );
    
    for (FailedEmail failed : toRetry) {
        try {
            emailService.sendEmail(failed.getEmail(), ...);
            failedEmailRepository.delete(failed);  // Success, remove from queue
            log.info(\"Retry succeeded for {}\", failed.getEmail());
            
        } catch (Exception e) {
            // Increment retry count
            failed.setRetryCount(failed.getRetryCount() + 1);
            
            if (failed.getRetryCount() >= 3) {
                // After 3 retries, notify admin
                adminService.notifyFailedEmail(failed);
                log.error(\"Email to {} failed after 3 retries\", failed.getEmail());
            } else {
                // Schedule next retry (exponential backoff)
                failed.setNextRetryTime(
                    LocalDateTime.now()
                        .plusMinutes(5L * (long)Math.pow(2, failed.getRetryCount()))
                );
            }
            
            failedEmailRepository.save(failed);
        }
    }
}
```

**Result:**
- User creates election results
- Results published immediately (10ms)
- If email fails: automatically retried
- After 3 retries: admin notified manually
- No data loss, no cascading failures
- Core election functionality unaffected

**Diagram:**
```
ElectionResultsPublished
├─ Save results ✓
├─ Publish event ✓
└─ Return to user immediately ✓
   ↓
Background thread:
├─ Send email #1 ✓
├─ Send email #2 ✓
├─ ...
├─ Send email #500 ✗ (CRASH)
│  └─ Catch exception
│     └─ Publish EmailFailedEvent
│        └─ Store in DB for retry
├─ Send email #501 ✓
└─ Continue...

Retry scheduler (every 60 seconds):
├─ Find failed emails with retry < 3
├─ Retry sending
├─ If succeed: remove from queue
└─ If fail 3 times: notify admin
```

This ensures **resilience**: system continues operating even if external service (email) fails."

