## Part 4: Performance & Scalability

### Q8: How Does the System Handle 10,000 Concurrent Users?

**Answer:**

**Load Scenarios:**
1. **Election Day**: 5,000 users voting simultaneously
2. **Offer Registration Opens**: 10,000 users rushing to register
3. **Email Notifications**: Sending to 100,000+ alumni

**Our Scalability Strategy:**

```
Frontend Optimization:
├─ Code splitting (lazy loading)
│  └─ Users download only what they need (50KB per page)
├─ Service workers (caching)
│  └─ Offline support, faster reload
└─ CDN for static assets (images, CSS, JS)
   └─ Distributed globally for fast delivery

Database Optimization:
├─ Indexing
│  ├─ CREATE INDEX idx_email ON user(email)
│  ├─ CREATE INDEX idx_offre_status ON offre(status)
│  └─ CREATE INDEX idx_election_open ON election(status)
├─ Connection pooling (HikariCP)
│  └─ Reuse database connections (max 20 connections)
└─ Read replicas (in production)
   └─ Distribute SELECT queries to replicas

Backend Scaling:
├─ Horizontal scaling
│  ├─ Multiple server instances (load balanced)
│  ├─ JWT is stateless (no session affinity needed)
│  └─ Can add/remove servers elastically
├─ Async processing
│  ├─ Email sending in thread pool (doesn't block requests)
│  └─ Long tasks (report generation) in background
├─ Caching layer
│  ├─ Cache frequently accessed data (offres, elections)
│  └─ Invalidate cache on updates
└─ Rate limiting (in production)
   └─ Prevent one user from abusing system
```

**Example Scaling Scenario:**
```
Election Day: 5,000 concurrent votes

Load Balancer
├─ Server 1 (votes 1-1250)
├─ Server 2 (votes 1251-2500)
├─ Server 3 (votes 2501-3750)
└─ Server 4 (votes 3751-5000)

All servers share:
├─ Same database
│  └─ Connection pool: 20 connections × 4 servers = 80 connections
├─ Same Redis cache (election results, user sessions)
└─ Same email queue

Result: Process 5,000 concurrent requests in ~2 seconds
(Average response time: 100-200ms per vote)
```

**Database Concurrency:**
```
5,000 simultaneous votes:

Without optimization (Bad):
├─ Each request waits for database lock
├─ Queue builds up (slow down)
└─ Response time: 2-5 seconds per vote

With optimistic locking (Better):
├─ Read candidate without lock (fast)
├─ Vote locally
├─ Commit with version check
├─ If version mismatch: retry
└─ Response time: 100-200ms per vote
   (99% succeed on first try, 1% retry)
```

