#### **Q11: How do you handle XSS (Cross-Site Scripting) attacks?**

**Answer:**
```html
<!-- ❌ Vulnerable: User-provided content directly in HTML -->
<p>{{ user.bio }}</p>  <!-- If bio = \"<img src=x onerror='alert(1)'>\", executes! -->

<!-- ✅ Safe: Angular auto-escapes content -->
<p [innerText]=\"user.bio\"></p>  <!-- Displays as text, not HTML -->

<!-- ✅ Or use DomSanitizer for rich text -->
<p [innerHTML]=\"sanitizer.sanitize(SecurityContext.HTML, user.bio)\"></p>
```

**Backend:**
```java
// Validate & sanitize HTML input
@Component
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class HtmlSanitizer {
    
    private final HtmlPolicy policy = new HtmlPolicyBuilder()
        .allowElements(\"b\", \"i\", \"u\", \"p\", \"br\")
        .allowAttributes(\"class\", \"id\").onElements(\"p\")
        .disallowElements(\"script\", \"iframe\", \"img\")  // ← Block dangerous tags
        .toFactory()
        .sanitize(...);
    
    public String sanitizeHtml(String html) {
        return policy.sanitize(html);
    }
}
